# Skilleraa — Engineering Review & Scorecard

## Before writing ANY code (mandatory)
Search and read first. Check every item:

| Check | Where to look |
|-------|----------------|
| Existing implementation | Related `pages/`, `components/`, `lib/`, `backend/`, migrations |
| Duplicate logic | Same flow already solved elsewhere |
| Duplicate API | FastAPI routers + `lib/*Service.js` + existing endpoints |
| Duplicate component | `components/` + layout shells |
| Duplicate SQL | `supabase/migrations/` tables, policies, RPCs |
| Existing utility | `lib/uiClasses.js`, `lib/logger.js`, helpers |
| Existing hook / context | `context/`, any `use*` patterns in src |
| Existing service | `lib/*Service.js`, `profilesService`, payments, storage |

**Rule:** If an existing implementation is found → **MODIFY IT**.  
Do **not** create another implementation, file, API, or migration that duplicates it.

Also verify: build plan, security (RLS/authz/secrets), performance, mobile.

## After completing work (mandatory scorecard)
Always report (0–100 integers + one-line rationale each):

1. **Project Health Score** — overall production readiness of touched area  
2. **Architecture Score** — fit with existing modules / no duplication  
3. **Security Score** — authz, RLS, secrets, uploads, admin  
4. **Performance Score** — queries, bundle, re-renders  
5. **Code Quality Score** — clarity, DRY, error/loading/empty states  
6. **Build Status** — `lint` / `build` / backend import (pass|fail|not run)  
7. **Git Recommendation** — exact `git add` / `git commit -m "…"` (never push unless asked)

## Severity when reviewing
**Critical** → auth bypass, payment forge, secret leak, RLS gap, data loss  
**High** → IDOR, missing role checks, CORS, unsafe uploads  
**Medium** → missing states, noisy queries, a11y  
**Low** → naming, dead imports, copy  

## Done means
No TODOs/placeholders · no UI redesign unless requested · additive migrations · modify-over-create respected  
